      "content": "First, you must notify the French data protection authority (CNIL) within 72 hours of discovering the breach, even if the potential high-risk impact isn't fully clear yet. You are also legally obligated to inform affected customers directly unless the breach is unlikely to affect them or they already know it. To avoid these consequences, ensure you have a formal incident response plan that defines who to contact, how to contain the breach technically, and strict protocols for documenting every step taken immediately after discovery.",
